## Methodology

{% if scoring_mode == "multibagger" %}
- **Scoring mode:** Multibagger Quality Score (7 pillars).
- **Pillar weights** ({{ profile_id }}): {{ pillar_weights }}
- Pillar scores are computed deterministically from yfinance `.info` (Tier-A)
  and annual income/balance/cash-flow statements (Tier-B), **percentile-ranked
  within GICS sector** (fallback to whole universe when peers < 6), then
  coverage-shrunk toward the median. A hard **red-flag veto pass** (structural
  cash burn, earnings-not-cash-backed, Beneish M > -1.78, Altman Z" < 1.1,
  insolvency-risk debt, promoter pledge, auditor flag, perception-only
  re-rating, working-capital trap) is applied after ranking. Tier-C governance
  data is never fabricated - it defaults to neutral and is surfaced as a manual
  checklist. LLM analysts *interpret* the numbers; they never produce them.
{% else %}
- **Factor weights** ({{ profile_id }}): {{ factor_weights }}
- Quality, Value, Momentum, Financial Health, Earnings Quality factors are
  computed deterministically from yfinance data and percentile-ranked across
  the candidate universe. LLM analysts then *interpret* the rankings; they do
  not produce numerical values.
{% endif %}
- See README.md for the full architecture.

